{"summary": "Fixed the bug in `separability_matrix` function where nested CompoundModels were not computing separability correctly. The issue was in the `_cstack` function in `/testbed/astropy/modeling/separable.py`, specifically in how it handled ndarray right operands. 

The original code incorrectly set `cright[-right.shape[0]:, -right.shape[1]:] = 1`, which replaced the actual coordinate matrix data with all True values, losing the internal separability structure of nested compound models. The fix changes this to `cright[-right.shape[0]:, :right.shape[1]] = right`, which properly copies the coordinate matrix data from the right operand.

This ensures that when processing nested compound models like `m.Pix2Sky_TAN() & (m.Linear1D(10) & m.Linear1D(5))`, the separability matrix correctly shows that the Linear1D components remain separable from each other, matching the behavior of the non-nested case.", "final_verification": {"checks": ["cd /testbed && python -c "from astropy.modeling import models as m; from astropy.modeling.separable import separability_matrix; cm = m.Linear1D(10) & m.Linear1D(5); result = separability_matrix(m.Pix2Sky_TAN() & cm); expected = [[True, True, False, False], [True, True, False, False], [False, False, True, False], [False, False, False, True]]; import numpy as np; assert np.array_equal(result, expected), f'Expected {expected}, got {result}'"", "cd /testbed && python -m pytest astropy/modeling/tests/test_separable.py"]}}

